Looking at this vulnerability, the issue is that credentials are stored in Python pickle format, which is vulnerable to arbitrary code execution through deserialization. The fix requires converting this to a JSON-based format.

Here is the corrected `credentials.token` file in JSON format, preserving the same credential data:

{"token_uri": "https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token", "client_secret": "SnpCAIq3fTuTfTC1vrRZb25t", "id_token": null, "token": "ya29.GlssB0vVe1SqwXcCb0k46x6"}